      "explanation": "In Formaldehyde (HCHO) both side of the C atom H presents but in Acetaldehyde (CH<sub>3</sub>CHO) one side of C atom -CH<sub>3</sub> group and other side H atom presents. So Formaldehyde is less crowded then it is more reactive.\n<br><br>CH<sub>3</sub>OH is 1<sup>o</sup> alcohol and t<sub>BuOH</sub> is 3<sup>o</sup> alcohol. As we know on 3<sup>o</sup> alcohol steric hindrance is very high compare to 1<sup>o</sup> alcohol and due to steric hindrance reactivity of 3<sup>o</sup> alcohol is less compare to 1<sup>o</sup> alcohol."
